    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66-a1">

                <pb facs="0213" n="79" xml:id="pg79"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                        709.—Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall to Señor Delgado.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 19,
                        1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>With reference to the affairs of Sagrini, the United States minister at Paris
                    says to the honorable Secretary of State, who concurs with him, that in his
                    opinion the Government of Salvador should authorize its minister there to offer
                    a reasonable sum to settle the claim, and in case of its non-acceptance by the
                    Italian Government then the good offices of the Government of the United States
                    might be offered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry C. Hall.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
